{"alignment":[{"from":["d1:REQ-1","d2:REQ-1","d3:REQ-1"],"mergedReq":"REQ-1"},{"from":["d1:REQ-2","d2:REQ-1"],"mergedReq":"REQ-2"},{"from":["d2:REQ-2","d3:REQ-3","d1:REQ-15"],"mergedReq":"REQ-3"},{"from":["d1:REQ-3","d2:REQ-3","d3:REQ-2"],"mergedReq":"REQ-4"},{"from":["d1:REQ-4","d2:REQ-4","d3:REQ-2"],"mergedReq":"REQ-5"},{"from":["d1:REQ-6","d2:REQ-5","d3:REQ-9"],"mergedReq":"REQ-6"},{"from":["d1:REQ-5","d2:REQ-6","d3:REQ-4"],"mergedReq":"REQ-7"},{"from":["d1:REQ-16","d2:REQ-7","d3:REQ-4"],"mergedReq":"REQ-8"},{"from":["d1:REQ-7","d2:REQ-8","d3:REQ-5"],"mergedReq":"REQ-9"},{"from":["d1:REQ-7","d2:REQ-9","d3:REQ-5"],"mergedReq":"REQ-10"},{"from":["d1:REQ-8","d2:REQ-10","d3:REQ-6"],"mergedReq":"REQ-11"},{"from":["d1:REQ-9","d2:REQ-12","d3:REQ-7"],"mergedReq":"REQ-12"},{"from":["d1:REQ-10","d2:REQ-12","d3:REQ-7"],"mergedReq":"REQ-13"},{"from":["d1:REQ-10","d2:REQ-13","d3:REQ-8"],"mergedReq":"REQ-14"},{"from":["d1:REQ-11","d2:REQ-14","d3:REQ-9"],"mergedReq":"REQ-15"},{"from":["d1:REQ-12","d2:REQ-14","d3:REQ-10"],"mergedReq":"REQ-16"},{"from":["d1:REQ-13","d2:REQ-15","d3:REQ-10"],"mergedReq":"REQ-17"},{"from":["d1:REQ-14","d2:REQ-16","d3:REQ-11"],"mergedReq":"REQ-18"}],"conflicts":["REQ-1 follows d1 and d3's contract-path reading without specifying an `/api` prefix; REQ-2 preserves d2's explicit reading that the locked operations are under `/api`. Resolve the contract path-prefix interpretation before implementation acceptance.","REQ-5.2 captures the assigned-warehouse restriction from d1/d3; REQ-5.5 captures d2's explicit Quality Manager/Auditor cross-warehouse read exception. These access-scope readings conflict and require contract clarification.","REQ-8.1 and REQ-8.3 capture expiry transition at the end of the expiry date (d1/d3); REQ-8.2 captures transition once the unit has passed its expiry date (d2). Clarify the exact scheduled transition boundary."],"spec":{"assumptions":["Customer authentication uses email and password followed by email-delivered one-time-code verification; password reset uses an email link.","Staff identity-provider URL, email sender, database connection, warehouse cut-off, safety margin, local time zone, working-day calendar, and holiday calendar are supplied by deployment or existing warehouse configuration rather than new configuration APIs.","Expiry processing is an application-side scheduled check and records dispatcher alerts; test time may be controlled.","The existing root health response, generated OpenAPI document, and Swagger UI remain available.","Temperature-history and excursion behavior operates on data available through contracted receipt logger uploads and persisted contracted records; no uncontracted logger-ingestion endpoint is introduced.","No legacy data is imported; business records are entered through contracted operations."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"No later than 120 seconds after the triggering reading is received.","text":"Excursion alerts are sent through the configured email channel to the driver when applicable, dispatcher, and warehouse Quality Officers after the triggering reading is received."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"5,000 devices reporting at once.","text":"The temperature-data processing capability supports logger and cold-room readings from concurrently reporting devices."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"100% of audit rows created by consequential-operation tests have non-empty actor and event-time fields; 0 audit rows are automatically expired.","text":"Consequential-operation audit events contain an actor and event time and are retained without automatic expiry."}],"outOfScope":["Portal, customer-portal, staff web, and mobile-application screens or client-side offline storage; this run implements the API side only.","Uncontracted API operations and broader workflows not exposed by contracts/openapi.yaml.","Legacy spreadsheet or paper-process data migration.","SMS and push notification delivery, social sign-in, alternate single sign-on, and vendor-specific logger clients.","An additional general inbound logger or temperature-ingestion API not present in the locked contract."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"Every operation in the locked contract has a valid authorized request and record fixtures.","id":"AC-REQ-1.1","level":"api","then":"The response status, media type, and body fields match the operation's declared successful response.","when":"A client calls each declared operation using its method, path, parameters, headers, and request media type."},{"given":"An operation declares invalid-input, authentication, authorization, not-found, conflict, or server-error responses.","id":"AC-REQ-1.2","level":"api","then":"The response status and error body match a response declared for that operation.","when":"The corresponding condition is sent through that operation."},{"given":"A path and method are absent from the locked contract.","id":"AC-REQ-1.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 404 or 405 and no business record is created.","when":"A request is sent to that path and method."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall implement every method, path, parameter, header, request and response schema, media type, and status defined in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, without adding uncontracted business operations.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-2","Q-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API is running.","id":"AC-REQ-2.1","level":"api","then":"Each response status is 200, the root response value is `API is up`, and the OpenAPI response includes the contracted `/api` operations.","when":"A client calls `/`, `/openapi/v1.json`, and `/swagger`."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall implement the locked contract under the `/api` path prefix, expose no uncontracted business operation, and preserve the existing root health response, OpenAPI document, and Swagger UI.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-2","Q-1","ASM-7"],"stability":0.6666666666666666},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A valid contracted create or update request is made against a configured database.","id":"AC-REQ-3.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is successful and the returned record fields match the persisted row.","when":"The request succeeds, the application restarts, and the resource is fetched through its contracted read operation."},{"given":"A contracted upload operation receives a valid evidence or logger file.","id":"AC-REQ-3.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is successful and the returned file or record fields match the uploaded content and metadata.","when":"The API restarts and the related contracted read or download operation is called."},{"given":"Legacy spreadsheet or paper-process data exists outside a new configured database and has not been submitted through contracted operations.","id":"AC-REQ-3.3","level":"api","then":"The database contains no imported legacy business row and response lists contain no imported legacy records.","when":"The API starts and contracted collections are queried."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall persist records, relationships, state changes, and file artifacts required by contracted operations in the configured shared database, keep successful mutations available after process restart, and not import legacy spreadsheet or paper-process business data.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","Q-1","Q-7","ASM-2"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active customer account has valid credentials and configured email delivery.","id":"AC-REQ-4.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains a challenge identifier, an email message contains the one-time code, and no authenticated customer result is issued before code verification.","when":"The customer submits credentials to the contracted sign-in operation."},{"given":"A customer challenge is pending.","id":"AC-REQ-4.2","level":"api","then":"Each response status and returned authentication or challenge value reflects the contract-defined outcome, and only a valid unused code produces an authenticated customer result.","when":"The customer verifies a valid code, submits an invalid or reused code, or requests a resend."},{"given":"A customer account requests a password reset.","id":"AC-REQ-4.3","level":"api","then":"The response values identify token usability, the reset link is sent by email, and a consumed or invalid token cannot reset the password again.","when":"The account requests, inspects, and completes a reset using the issued token."},{"given":"The staff identity-provider authorization URL is configured.","id":"AC-REQ-4.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned value is the configured URL.","when":"An unauthenticated client calls the staff authorization-URL operation."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall provide contracted staff authorization-URL lookup, customer email-and-password sign-in with one-time-code verification and resend, and password-reset request, token-inspection, and completion flows, delivering customer codes and reset links by email.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","ASM-1","ASM-9"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Customer organisations have separate orders, deliveries, certificates, or recall records.","id":"AC-REQ-5.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 or the contract-defined not-found status and contains no other-organisation record.","when":"An authenticated user from one organisation lists or requests another organisation's records."},{"given":"A staff member is assigned to one warehouse and another warehouse has records.","id":"AC-REQ-5.2","level":"api","then":"The response list contains only assigned-warehouse records and an inaccessible-record response contains no record value.","when":"The staff member lists or requests warehouse-scoped stock, receipts, orders, routes, or quality records outside the assignment."},{"given":"An Auditor is authenticated and a record is available.","id":"AC-REQ-5.3","level":"api","then":"The read response contains the record and each prohibited write response status is 403.","when":"The Auditor reads the record and attempts a contracted create, update, or delete operation."},{"given":"An account has been deactivated or removed.","id":"AC-REQ-5.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 401 or 403 and contains no protected record.","when":"That account makes a subsequent authenticated request to a protected contracted operation."},{"given":"A Quality Manager or Auditor is authenticated and requests a record in a warehouse outside an ordinary staff member's assignment.","id":"AC-REQ-5.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is successful and the returned record belongs to the requested warehouse.","when":"The account reads that record."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall enforce contracted customer-organisation, staff-role, warehouse-scope, Auditor read-only, and account-status restrictions on every operation, including denial of access to deactivated accounts.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","Q-2"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A System Administrator creates or searches for a product.","id":"AC-REQ-6.1","level":"api","then":"The response record contains the submitted product specification and active state, and searches return matching product records.","when":"The product is submitted, listed, retrieved, or deactivated through contracted operations."},{"given":"A product has no valid temperature profile or a profile has overlapping or discontinuous tier boundaries.","id":"AC-REQ-6.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 and the response error identifies the invalid profile or tier values.","when":"The product or profile is submitted."},{"given":"A valid profile change includes an effective date, label, limits, tiers, and reason.","id":"AC-REQ-6.3","level":"api","then":"The response record and profile list contain the new version, reason, effective date, and actor, while the previous version remains returned unchanged.","when":"A System Administrator creates the profile version and later lists versions."},{"given":"A product has an earlier profile version.","id":"AC-REQ-6.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the earlier profile record remains unchanged.","when":"A caller attempts to alter that earlier version rather than create a new version."},{"given":"A product is deactivated.","id":"AC-REQ-6.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 or 409 as declared by the operation and the response does not report a successful order.","when":"A customer submits an order line for that product."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall persist searchable products and immutable versioned temperature profiles, require a profile for each product, and validate profile tiers and governance history.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","Q-1","Q-5"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A permitted Warehouse Operator submits a valid receipt with product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, and location.","id":"AC-REQ-7.1","level":"api","then":"The response record contains the submitted values and a Quarantined status.","when":"The operator creates the receipt and retrieves it."},{"given":"A product and lot number already have a receipt.","id":"AC-REQ-7.2","level":"api","then":"The response contains a distinct receipt identifier and the stock list reports both quantities without merging receipt records.","when":"A second permitted receipt with the same product and lot number is submitted."},{"given":"A receipt expiry date is before the current date, or release is attempted when expiry is within 30 days of receipt.","id":"AC-REQ-7.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 or 409 as defined by the operation and the receipt or release status value is not changed to Released.","when":"The receipt or release action is submitted."},{"given":"A valid supplier-format logger file or separate evidence file is available for an existing receipt.","id":"AC-REQ-7.4","level":"api","then":"The response contains the receipt record or action result and a subsequent receipt response contains the stored file-related record or processed readings.","when":"The file is uploaded through its contracted receipt operation and the receipt is subsequently fetched."},{"given":"A handling unit has positive available quantity at a warehouse location.","id":"AC-REQ-7.5","level":"api","then":"The response record contains the resulting quantity and location, and a movement record contains actor, time, source, destination, and moved quantity.","when":"A permitted move or opening-stock operation is submitted."},{"given":"An authorized Quality Officer records a release decision for a quarantined receipt.","id":"AC-REQ-7.6","level":"api","then":"The response record shows the decision actor and time and the stock status is Released.","when":"The contracted quality disposition workflow records the decision."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall persist separate contracted receipt, receipt-logger, receipt-evidence, stock, movement, and opening-stock records and enforce receipt traceability, quarantine, expiry validation, and Quality Officer release.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","Q-2","Q-3","Q-7"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A handling unit is allocated and reaches the end of its expiry date.","id":"AC-REQ-8.1","level":"job","then":"The database row has Expired status, the order response no longer lists that allocation, an audit event records the change, and an alert email call is recorded for the dispatcher.","when":"The scheduled expiry check runs."},{"given":"A released handling unit has passed its expiry date and is allocated to an order.","id":"AC-REQ-8.2","level":"job","then":"The stock row status is Expired, the allocation count for that unit is zero, and an alert row identifies the dispatcher notification.","when":"The scheduled expiry check runs."},{"given":"Stock reaches the end of its expiry date under controlled test time.","id":"AC-REQ-8.3","level":"job","then":"The stock row has Expired status, its allocation row is removed, and a dispatcher alert row records the expiry outcome.","when":"The scheduled expiry check runs."}],"ears":"When a handling unit reaches expiry, the Meridian API shall automatically mark it Expired, remove it from allocations, record the change, and alert the dispatcher through the contracted scheduled check.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","Q-3","ASM-5","ASM-10"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated customer submits an order with at least one line, positive pack quantities, an organisation-owned address, and an idempotency key.","id":"AC-REQ-9.1","level":"api","then":"Both response bodies return the same order identifier and the order list contains one order.","when":"The order is submitted twice with the same key and payload."},{"given":"A customer submits an invalid line, another organisation's address, a date earlier than permitted, or a product inactive for ordering.","id":"AC-REQ-9.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 400 or 409 and no order row is created.","when":"The customer places the order."},{"given":"A valid configured warehouse cut-off, working-day calendar, holiday calendar, and warehouse time zone are available.","id":"AC-REQ-9.3","level":"api","then":"The response record accepts no date earlier than the next working day before cut-off or the working day after that when submitted after cut-off.","when":"A customer requests an order delivery date before or after cut-off."},{"given":"An order is not yet Packed or has already reached Packed status.","id":"AC-REQ-9.4","level":"api","then":"The response status and order status value reflect the applicable lifecycle rule, and successful cancellation returns the allocated quantity to available stock.","when":"The customer attempts to change or cancel it."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall persist customer orders and dispatch allocations using the serving warehouse's configured cut-off, working-day, holiday, time-zone, and customer shelf-life rules, and enforce idempotency, order validation, pre-packing customer changes, and cancellation rules.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","Q-2","Q-4","Q-5","ASM-6","ASM-11"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Released stock is available for an order from its serving warehouse and has eligible lots.","id":"AC-REQ-10.1","level":"api","then":"The response record shows earliest-expiry eligible lots first, applies minimum remaining shelf life, uses greater stability-budget usage first for tied expiry dates, and exposes each allocation and outstanding quantity.","when":"The order is allocated."},{"given":"Suitable stock is insufficient for a partial order or any line of a complete-only order.","id":"AC-REQ-10.2","level":"api","then":"The partial order response shows allocated and outstanding quantities without over-allocating stock, while the complete-only order holds no stock until every line can be fully allocated.","when":"Allocation is attempted."},{"given":"Multiple orders are submitted concurrently against the same available handling units.","id":"AC-REQ-10.3","level":"api","then":"The response records and stock list show no unit allocated to more than one order and total allocated quantity does not exceed physical available quantity.","when":"The allocations are committed."},{"given":"A dispatcher submits an allocation override with a reason, without a reason, or to stock violating Released status or customer shelf life.","id":"AC-REQ-10.4","level":"api","then":"The valid response record includes the reason and changed allocation, while each invalid response status is 400 or 409 and the original allocation remains unchanged.","when":"The override operation is called."},{"given":"Suitable stock is released for waiting back orders.","id":"AC-REQ-10.5","level":"api","then":"The order response records show oldest-first back-order allocation.","when":"The allocation service updates affected orders."},{"given":"An older back order awaits suitable stock or a complete-only order cannot be fully allocated.","id":"AC-REQ-10.6","level":"api","then":"The response record shows eligible back orders filled in submission order and no stock held by the incomplete complete-only order.","when":"Suitable stock is released or allocation is attempted."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall allocate only released, physically available stock meeting customer minimum remaining shelf life, select earliest expiry first with the specified stability-budget tie-break, and apply complete-order, partial-order, back-order, and override rules.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","Q-4","Q-5"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Warehouse Operator submits a pack request for allocated stock.","id":"AC-REQ-11.1","level":"api","then":"The response record contains the box, logger, lot quantities, operator, and seal time; a reused logger or incompatible packing response status is 409.","when":"The requested box contains one logger, products with the same storage band, and a compatible box type."},{"given":"A dispatcher submits a route with date, vehicle, driver, ordered stops, and planned arrival times.","id":"AC-REQ-11.2","level":"api","then":"The response record contains the requested route values and a conflicting driver or vehicle assignment returns status 409.","when":"The route is created, updated, or confirmed."},{"given":"A route's packed box would exceed qualified duration less the configured safety margin at a planned arrival.","id":"AC-REQ-11.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the response message identifies the box and qualification shortfall or duration overrun.","when":"The route confirmation operation is called."},{"given":"A driver calls route listing, route detail, scan, departure, or synchronization operations for the authenticated driver's route.","id":"AC-REQ-11.4","level":"api","then":"The response list or record contains only that driver's authorized route, ordered stops, expected boxes, scans, and departure state.","when":"The driver supplies contracted date, action identifiers, or route data."},{"given":"A driver synchronizes queued actions with distinct action identifiers or repeats an action identifier.","id":"AC-REQ-11.5","level":"api","then":"The response record contains accepted and conflicting actions, and the resulting route history contains each accepted action only once.","when":"The synchronization operation is called."},{"given":"A driver submits a handover with receiver, acknowledgement, signature, photo, completion time, and box delivery or refusal quantities.","id":"AC-REQ-11.6","level":"api","then":"The response record and delivery-evidence response contain persisted evidence and quantities, and refused quantities retain the refusal reason.","when":"The handover operation is called and authorized delivery evidence is subsequently fetched."},{"given":"A confirmed route is changed before its driver has left for the affected stop.","id":"AC-REQ-11.7","level":"api","then":"The response record contains the changed schedule or stop order and an email call or driver-change event is recorded.","when":"A dispatcher updates the route schedule or stop order."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall persist compatible box packing and route plans, enforce box and route qualification, and record driver loading, departure, synchronization, handover, refusal, and delivery-evidence operations.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","Q-1","Q-2","Q-5","ASM-3","ASM-6"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A contracted receipt logger upload contains repeated, late, out-of-order, future-dated, or pre-sealing readings.","id":"AC-REQ-12.1","level":"api","then":"The response record places readings at their occurred times, stores a duplicate once, flags future and pre-sealing readings as excluded from calculations, and shows unavailable-reading gaps.","when":"The file is processed and temperature history is requested for its entity and date range."},{"given":"Three consecutive in-band readings follow an out-of-band reading in persisted history.","id":"AC-REQ-12.2","level":"api","then":"The response records show the excursion open from the first out-of-band reading until the third consecutive in-band reading and show time charged to each applicable tier.","when":"The related temperature history and handling-unit record are requested."},{"given":"A handling unit has excursion history or a late reading changes that history.","id":"AC-REQ-12.3","level":"api","then":"The response record shows separate budgets for portions with different histories, updated remaining tier allowances, excursion links, holds, and an audit event for the correction.","when":"The handling-unit or temperature-history operation is called after recalculation."},{"given":"An excursion begins, a tier allowance falls below 25 percent, a tier is exhausted, or a not-permitted range is reached.","id":"AC-REQ-12.4","level":"api","then":"An email call is recorded for the required driver when on-route, dispatcher, and warehouse Quality Officers, and affected stock response records have On Hold status pending a decision.","when":"The triggering reading is received and processed."},{"given":"A logger has sent no reading for 15 minutes and its box is out for delivery.","id":"AC-REQ-12.5","level":"api","then":"The response record marks the device silent, shows the gap, and an alert email call is recorded.","when":"The silent-device check runs and temperature history is requested."},{"given":"A cold room or its temperature records are available.","id":"AC-REQ-12.6","level":"api","then":"The response list or record contains the latest reading, status, gaps, alerts, history timestamps, and applicable band and excursion markers.","when":"A caller lists cold rooms, retrieves a cold room, or requests temperature history for a room, box, lot, handling unit, or device."},{"given":"A handling unit has recorded temperature history with an interval containing no readings and a stored profile band.","id":"AC-REQ-12.7","level":"api","then":"The response contains readings in recorded-time order, an explicit gap, and temperature-band and excursion fields for the requested interval.","when":"The caller fetches temperature history for the unit or its box, lot, device, or cold room."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall expose temperature histories for contracted entity types and persist available logger readings, gaps, excursions, tier-by-tier handling-unit budgets, related holds, and corrected history when readings arrive late or out of order.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","Q-1","Q-3","ASM-4","ASM-8","ASM-10"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Quality Officer submits a disposition proposal with disposition, reason, and identity confirmation.","id":"AC-REQ-13.1","level":"api","then":"The response record contains the proposal and actor, the same officer cannot approve it, and a different eligible manager's approval or return is recorded without replacing the proposal.","when":"The proposal is retrieved or a decision is submitted by the proposing officer or an eligible different Quality Manager."},{"given":"A quality decision exists and an authorized caller submits a separately signed superseding decision.","id":"AC-REQ-13.2","level":"api","then":"The response record contains the new decision and the earlier decision remains available in the returned decision history.","when":"The supersede operation is called."},{"given":"Rejected stock has a positive quantity to destroy.","id":"AC-REQ-13.3","level":"api","then":"The response record contains those values and the destroyed quantity is removed from available stock.","when":"An authorized caller submits a destruction date, quantity, and witness."},{"given":"A handling unit has tiered budget usage and a related quality case.","id":"AC-REQ-13.4","level":"api","then":"The response contains the used and remaining value for each tier and linked case telemetry and decision fields.","when":"An authorized Quality Officer fetches the unit and quality case."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall persist quality cases, signed proposals and decisions, superseding decisions, and destruction records, applying the required two-person quality approval and decision-history rules.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","Q-2","Q-3","Q-5","Q-6"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An eligible Quality Manager starts a signed recall for selected product lots.","id":"AC-REQ-14.1","level":"api","then":"The response records identify affected stock, warehouse locations, boxes, routes, deliveries, customer response progress, and recalled held stock is unavailable for allocation.","when":"The recall is started and its record and trace are requested."},{"given":"A customer submits or updates a recall response for an authorized delivery.","id":"AC-REQ-14.2","level":"api","then":"The response record contains on-hand, used, destroyed, and stated-disposition values and recall progress reflects the submitted quantities.","when":"The recall response operation is called."},{"given":"A recall has unaccounted quantity or all quantity is accounted for.","id":"AC-REQ-14.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 for closure with unaccounted quantity and no valid write-off, or the response record contains the signed closure or write-off when preconditions are met.","when":"A Quality Manager submits closure or a signed write-off."},{"given":"A started recall has affected warehouse, box, route, and delivery records.","id":"AC-REQ-14.4","level":"api","then":"The response lists contain the chronological trace of the lot through warehouse, boxes, routes, deliveries, movements, and destruction records.","when":"Recall-trace and lot-history operations are called."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall persist signed recalls, trace selected lots through affected stock and delivery records, block affected stock still held, and record customer responses and signed closure or write-off decisions until quantities are accounted for.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","Q-1","Q-2","Q-3","Q-5","Q-6"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated customer requests orders, deliveries, delivery details, certificates, certificate files, or recall notices.","id":"AC-REQ-15.1","level":"api","then":"The response list, record, or PDF file contains only records belonging to that customer's organisation.","when":"The corresponding customer operation is called."},{"given":"A Customer Administrator submits a valid saved address or invitation, changes an address, or removes an address or team member within their organisation.","id":"AC-REQ-15.2","level":"api","then":"The response record or action result identifies the change and subsequent lists contain the updated organisation-scoped address or team record.","when":"The contracted customer-administration operation is called."},{"given":"A Customer Administrator attempts to edit or remove an address or member belonging to another organisation.","id":"AC-REQ-15.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 or the contract-defined not-found status and no other-organisation row is changed.","when":"The contracted customer-administration operation is called."},{"given":"An authenticated customer account has a saved language preference.","id":"AC-REQ-15.4","level":"api","then":"The response record contains the saved language value and a value outside the contract enum returns status 400.","when":"The account is retrieved and patched with `en` or `ar`."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall implement customer organisation account, address, team, delivery, certificate, recall-notice, order, and language-preference operations with returned records and mutations scoped to the authenticated organisation.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","Q-1","Q-2","ASM-1","ASM-9"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A System Administrator requests organisations, organization details, accounts, or account details.","id":"AC-REQ-16.1","level":"api","then":"The response list or record contains persisted organization, member, address, shelf-life, role, and access-assignment values within caller authorization scope.","when":"The corresponding list or retrieval operation is called."},{"given":"A System Administrator creates, updates, or deactivates an account or updates an organization's minimum remaining shelf life.","id":"AC-REQ-16.2","level":"api","then":"The response status and record or action result reflect the new account state, roles, assignments, or minimum shelf-life value.","when":"The contracted administration operation is called."},{"given":"An authorized caller requests an operational report for a permitted date range and warehouse or requests lot history.","id":"AC-REQ-16.3","level":"api","then":"The response record or list contains only authorized report values and chronologically ordered receipt, movement, delivery, and destruction events for the requested lot.","when":"The report or lot-history operation is called."}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall implement contracted administration, operational-report, and lot-history operations, persisting organisation shelf-life settings, account role and warehouse assignments, and chronological business records.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-3","Q-1","Q-2"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A consequential contracted change or decision is successfully recorded.","id":"AC-REQ-17.1","level":"api","then":"The response list contains the event's actor, timestamp, action type, affected record, and applies the supplied filters.","when":"An authorized caller queries audit events using supported search, date, action-type, or user filters."},{"given":"An audit event has been recorded.","id":"AC-REQ-17.2","level":"api","then":"The response list still contains the even